s, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and write, no newline. That changes body. Need keep same response bodies. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) for success. But if user struct with fields Name, Email", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0035596590023487806], [760, -6.753326892852783]], [[1144, -1.1444157280493528e-05], [14235, -12.353168487548828]], [[4087, -0.011670295149087906], [310, -4.634530067443848]], [[1156, -0.03510800749063492], [303, -3.619401454925537]], [[579, -0.22218629717826843], [25, -2.378047227859497]], [[1622, -0.003578681033104658], [3296, -6.400534152984619]], [[13, -0.3518783450126648], [25, -1.5647422075271606]], [[14235, -0.03457760065793991], [1165, -4.081655025482178]], [[89109, -0.32925689220428467], [7936, -1.7736786603927612]], [[5805, -0.00023993747890926898], [2400, -8.731534957885742]], [[9830, -0.02287130244076252], [6795, -3.8462069034576416]], [[6795, -2.837221290974412e-05], [17369, -11.884868621826172]], [[1083, -1.3963826894760132], [47781, -1.5904287099838257]], [[1228, -0.09678960591554642], [2400, -2.784287691116333]], [[470, -3.278309304732829e-05], [5568, -10.610076904296875]], [[5568, -0.0030872744973748922], [74243, -6.108014106750488]], [[440, -0.927302896976471], [25, -1.8665614128112793]], [[2708, -0.034746862947940826], [1